      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Severity: NC State calls all parts seriously toxic to dogs and cats but rates the poison low severity for people; the ASPCA genus entry (Schefflera, not S. arboricola by name) lists dogs and cats as toxic with burning mouth, drooling and vomiting. Graded 2 for pets and 1 for children by the agent; the 01e baseline was 1, so a reviewer may want to lower it. Size is the NC State indoor figure (4 to 6 ft tall and wide, upper value); RHS gives 0.5 to 1 m by 0.1 to 0.5 m. The RHS page makes no toxicity statement. Temperature and humidity: no usable figure. Pachira (money tree) is the non-toxic look-alike."
      },
